Unreleased
    * hpc: a new plugin, for HPC clusters, with completion for Slurm's
      sbatch, salloc, srun, squeue, scancel, sinfo and sacct: all
      their options (from Slurm 26.05.5's source, as --help leaves
      many out), and the partitions, accounts, QOS, nodes, features,
      GRES, licenses, reservations and jobs of the cluster, asked of
      it when Tab is pressed; srun and salloc hand the command they
      run over to its completer. extra.completion.all loads it; to
      have it alone, enable extra.completion.hpc
    * bio: completion for pyrodigal
    * bio: bwa-mem2 mem no longer offers a line of dashes as an option,
      nor -x, which it doesn't have; hmmscan --qformat completes the
      formats; kallisto's -g, -c and -p take a file, and its long
      options (--gtf, --tag, ...) get their values, as do DAS_Tool's
    * bio: the names of sequences (samtools faidx REF <Tab>, samtools
      view BAM <Tab>, -r) and of a VCF's samples are kept until the
      file changes, and are fast for an assembly's millions of contigs
      (they timed out); none are offered while more than 5000 match
    * science: a nextflow_schema.json that isn't valid JSON (one being
      edited) no longer breaks the completion of nextflow run

Version 0.7.0 2026-10-19 by luispedro
    * The first release. Releases are tags vX.Y.N, the Nth for luish
      X.Y, which luish 0.7's release = "luish" takes: to stay on them
      (rather than main, which may need a newer luish), add the source
      as extra = { gh = "luispedro/luish-extra", release = "luish" }
    * Faster Tab where completion parsed the same text at each Tab:
      LibreOffice's formats and filters (50 ms to 2 ms), mpv's options
      (100 ms to 15 ms), ffmpeg's codecs, filters and private options,
      claude's commands, ruff's rule codes
    * Needs luish 0.7.0 or later (luish-version = "0.7" in every
      plugin.toml), for sh::glob
    * Files by extension (FASTA, BAM, index prefixes, ...) are listed
      much faster, with luish's sh::glob
    * media: a new plugin, for audio and video, with completion for
      ffmpeg: the options of an input or an output (ffmpeg's own and
      the generic ones of libavcodec and libavformat, from ffmpeg
      9.0.2), with stream specifiers (-c:v, -metadata:s:a) and the
      private options of the codecs and the format chosen (-c:v
      libx264 -preset, -f mp4 -movflags), read from the installed
      ffmpeg, as are the codecs, formats, filters and pixel formats;
      filtergraphs (-vf scale=w=1280:in_range=full) and the streams of
      the inputs for -map (with ffprobe). extra.completion.all loads
      it; to have it alone, enable extra.completion.media
    * system: completion for git-annex, by git-annex itself (its
      commands, options, remotes, backends and files), also as git annex
    * bio: completion for amrfinder (AMRFinderPlus, with the taxonomy
      groups of the installed database for --organism) and
      amrfinder_update
    * bio: completion for eggnog-mapper (emapper.py, with its taxonomic
      scopes for --tax_scope; download_eggnog_data.py, create_dbs.py,
      hmm_mapper.py)
    * bio: completion for vsearch and for cd-hit (cd-hit, cd-hit-est,
      cd-hit-2d, cd-hit-est-2d, cd-hit-454)
    * conda: looks for conda in PATH without forking, in every shell
    * themes: gruvbox and solarized give operators and redirections
      (|, &&, >) a colour of the palette (gruvbox's text colour,
      solarized's emphasized grey), not the terminal's bold default,
      which some terminals drew too dark
    * complete/ is now completion/, as std's completion plugin: the
      plugins are extra/completion/bio, ... (were extra/complete/bio);
      config.toml needs the new names (extra.completion.all = "*")
